<p>If the user authentication settings have been made on the printer, you 
 also need to make the user authentication settings on the printer driver. 
 After selecting the <span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication</span> to <span class="Term-Soft">On</span>, enter a login name and password in the <span class="Term-Soft">Authentication</span> 
 dialog box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> tab.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/PCL_CS/IDH_HOW_AUTHENTICATION">Using User Authentication</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about user authentication, see the 
 operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="authonoff" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication</span></p>
<p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">On</span> to print using user authentication.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="dispauth" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Display [Authentication] Dialog Before Print</span></p>
<p>Select this check box to display the <span class="Term-Soft">Authentication</span> dialog box before printing.</p>
<p>After you enable the function, select whether to display a dialog box every time or to display it only when <span class="Term-Soft">Login User Name</span> is blank.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="credentials" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Display [Authentication] Dialog Before Printing for Windows Credentials</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to display the <span class="Term-Soft">Authentication</span> dialog box for Windows credentials.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="encryptlogin" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Encrypt Login Password</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to encrypt the login password when sending it to the machine.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="driverencryptkey" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Driver Encryption Key:</span></p>
<p>To encrypt the login password when sending it to the printer, enter the driver encryption key already set on the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="reenterkey" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Reenter the Confirmation Key:</span></p>
<p>Enter the login password again for confirmation.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The optional network data protection unit must 
 be installed.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this dialog box to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
